@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# Spike 23: the web page over today's certificate
+
+**Not run.** No browser was driven when the web control surface was
+built, so every line under "What to see" is open and the answers rest
+on the owner's phone. Nothing in the page depends on one of them
+turning out a particular way; each says what the build does instead.
+
+## Questions
+
+1. Does a `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict` cookie named
+   `__Host-sb-<server id>`, set by a reply from a user-accepted
+   self-signed certificate with no subject alternative name on an
+   IP-literal host, get stored and sent back by Chrome and by Safari?
+   (`docs/remote-client.md` §5; the plan's Unresolved 3.) If not, the
+   cookie transport does not work in that browser and the fallback is
+   the owner's call, not a second transport built now.
+2. Do two servers on one address and two ports, each setting a cookie
+   under its own server id, keep both cookies?
+3. Does `connect-src 'self'` admit `wss://` to the same host in each
+   browser? If not, the socket is what is lost and the 3 s poll carries.
+4. Does a page load of three requests plus a stray `/favicon.ico` fit
+   the 4-connection pool when the browser opens five parallel
+   connections? Pages answer `Connection: close`, so each frees its slot.
+
+## How to see it
+
+Use the real app against a scratch data directory, so nothing touches
+the owner's paired devices (keep the path short; the wake socket has a
+104-byte limit):
+
+```sh
+SWITCHBOARD_DATA_DIR=/tmp/sb23 SWITCHBOARD_TMUX_SOCKET=switchboard-test-23 cargo run --locked
+```
+
+In Settings, open Remote devices, turn on network listening, allow
+pairing, and open the URL under the QR (Copy invite) in the browser on
+the Mac or the phone. Proceed past the certificate warning. For
+question 2 start a second copy with `SWITCHBOARD_DATA_DIR=/tmp/sb23b`
+and a different port, and pair it in the same browser.
+
+For question 4, with the app running, from another shell:
+
+```sh
+for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do curl -sk -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://127.0.0.1:<port>/ & done; wait
+```
+
+## What to see
+
+| Question | Chrome (Mac) | Safari (Mac) | Safari (iPhone) |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Warning offers a way past | not run | not run | not run |
+| Cookie stored and sent | not run | not run | not run |
+| Two cookies kept | not run | not run | not run |
+| `wss://` admitted | not run | not run | not run |
+| Five parallel connections | not run | not run | not run |
